source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Both marker runs are read inside the cell: Jira renders one data cell holding a square list whose only item is `a` with a forced newline, and a square list nested in that item holding `b`. jiro reads the row across both lines and keeps the whole table as raw Jira Markup, which a GFM cell could hold none of.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|- a\\
-- b|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><ul class="alternate" type="square">
	<li>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />
	<ul class="alternate" type="square">
		<li>b</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|- a\\
-- b|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
